# loft registry — 58 available packages
# install: `loft install <name>`   ·   surface: `loft api <name>`

arguments 0.2.8 — CLI argument parsing — positional args + flags + auto-generated --help.
assets 0.5.2 — A game's content pack that IS a loft store — art, audio and the scenes that place them, range-read off a static file server.  No codec, no parse step, no server-side code.
audio 0.2.3 — Clips, voices and one mix: the same sound on a PC and on a 32-bit device
audio_bus 0.2.0 — A mixer for game audio — buses that multiply, and a duck that restores exactly
cbor 0.1.13 — Signable canonical CBOR (RFC 8949), pure loft — canonical map-key ordering, full decode, byte-identical encode->decode->encode, native == wasm.
crypto 0.4.4 — SHA-256, HMAC, HKDF, AES-256-GCM, Ed25519, ECDSA P-256, X25519, HPKE, base64 and hex: one C source on every target, native == wasm
drawing 0.5.1 — Render a .draw scene — a sprite authored as lines of text — pixel-identically to the Python renderer it replaces
fixstep 0.1.4 — A fixed simulation step in exact integer time — clock, bank, one-shot timer
game_protocol 0.1.8 — The message types a multiplayer game's client and server share — envelopes, kinds and constructors; pure loft, transport-agnostic
glb 0.1.8 — glTF 2.0 binary (.glb) writer — exports Mesh / Scene as a glb file readable by Blender, three.js, gltf-validator.  Standalone (pure-loft, no GPU).
gpu 0.3.1 — Drawing on a GPU through pipelines, passes and uniform blocks, with no graphics stack named: a backend library beneath it draws
gpu_gl 0.2.3 — The OpenGL backend of gpu: OpenGL 3.3 on Linux and macOS, OpenGL ES 3 on Android, WebGL2 in a page
gpu_host 0.1.0 — Opens a gpu device on the backend this machine has: Metal on a Mac, OpenGL elsewhere and where Metal is absent, Vulkan on Linux by name
gpu_metal 0.1.1 — The Metal backend of gpu: a Mac's GPU through Metal, in a window of its own
gpu_paint 0.2.0 — Rectangles, images and sprites at pixel positions, drawn through gpu: a painter and sprite sheets for any backend
gpu_record 0.2.0 — A GPU backend that draws nothing and writes down every call it receives: for testing a program's drawing on a machine with no display
gpu_vulkan 0.1.2 — The Vulkan backend of gpu: Vulkan 1.3 on Linux, in an X11 window
graphics 0.13.3 — A 2D canvas, windows, OpenGL and text for loft (meshes and glTF are mesh3d and glb)
gridmesh 0.2.7 — Chunk-local mesh-generation primitives for world-building algorithms.
hex_body 0.3.6 — The moving body — rigs, revolute joints with computed limits, pure poses, and collision proxies. hexbody's own body model, part of the hex_* family.
hex_draw 0.1.10 — Draw a model into the field, and read its wall surface back.
hex_edge 0.2.7 — Collision as an edge set, and the analytic surfaces behind it.
hex_field 0.1.11 — Exact-integer hex cell sets and their outlines — the base of the hex_* family.
hex_fit 0.1.6 — The doorstep — refuse at authoring time what would not round-trip.
hex_form 0.1.9 — The exact turtle form on the hex lattice, and its canonical text.
hex_grid 0.1.4 — Hex-grid geometry — pointy-top, ODD-R OFFSET coordinates: coordinate/pixel conversion, neighbours, distance, corners and canonical edges, plus a square local basis for right-angled structures placed on the hex world.
hex_ground 0.1.2 — The ground of one place: a height and a surface kind per cell, shaped into terraces, a hill, a seat, a cut and cliffs
hex_place 0.1.7 — Place, seat and combine — the operations a model survives.
hex_recover 0.1.7 — Rebuild a model from the field — exactly, or with a reported residual.
hex_roof 0.1.10 — Roof profiles as a height field, and the fit that recovers them.
hex_shape 0.1.10 — The line primitive, the box and the arc — the shape vocabulary of the hex_* family.
hex_terrain 0.1.8 — The OVERLAND terrain layer of the `hex_*` family: a coarse overland hex lattice
hex_way 0.1.7 — A way is an exact centreline plus offsets, never a rasterised band.
hex_world 0.2.3 — Sparse 32x32-chunk hex-grid world data model — Cell / Chunk / World with binary save/load.
html 0.1.3 — HTML escaping helpers for loft.
imaging 0.5.3 — PNG load/save and pixel manipulation for loft: one C source on every target, no Rust crate
input 0.3.1 — Game input for loft — action/axis bindings resolved to per-tick input state.
lavition_ui ? — Panel layout, hit-testing and text metrics for an in-engine editor UI: rectangles and hits, with no world, no lattice, no window and no GL.
loft 2026.11.0 — The loft toolchain: compiler, interpreter and standard library.
markdown 0.2.5 — Markdown-to-HTML rendering for loft — headings, inline spans, slugify, link rewriting.
mesh3d 0.1.5 — 3D geometry primitives — Vec/Mat, Mesh, Scene, Camera, Light.  Standalone (pure-loft, no GPU).
pluginabi 0.1.10 — Plugin call protocol — the six-operation contract (initial_state / apply_op / make_op / render / snapshot / load_snapshot) as canonical-CBOR frames over a byte channel. Not a runtime, ABI or sandbox: loft already provides those.
random 0.5.2 — PRNGs in three tiers: a shared PCG-64 with rand_seed reproducibility, owned RandStream streams, and a 32-bit tier
regex 0.6.1 — Small-script regex: `search`, `matches`, `capture` / `capture_all` with groups, `replace_on` and a lazy `split_on`, with a cache of compiled patterns.
scene3d 0.6.0 — A 3D scene a game's view gives once — tiles of faces, the cells' light, actors — drawn through gpu
screen 0.2.1 — A small frame on the machine's screen, scaled up, with the keys of its window — one API on a desktop and a device
script 0.4.0 — What a script reaches for, on demand: a recursive walk (lazy, or sorted), a copy, a glob, a set of texts — each a method that loads the library on use.
server 0.7.6 — HTTP + WebSocket server for loft — the natives are loft's `net` component, so the package builds no crate.
shapes 0.5.4 — 2D geometry primitives — Rect, Circle, overlap tests, clamp.  Pure-loft, no other deps.
ssh 0.1.5 — SSH client for loft — drive an interactive remote shell (e.g. attach tmux) over password auth, never stored. Native-only.
stage 0.20.1 — A retained 2-D scene for loft: a node tree you mutate, with transforms, clipping, batching, pointer routing and widget states
text2d 0.4.7 — Text that always draws — a built-in face, a glyph atlas, measured metrics, wrapping and alignment, with no font file and no GL context
tile_world 0.14.0 — An unbounded, layered square-grid world, and the routines that answer questions about it: paths, sight and light
tiles 0.7.0 — Tile sheets, map layers and sprites drawn at a surface's own resolution through a camera
time 0.4.1 — Date/time arithmetic on millisecond-since-epoch integers — proleptic Gregorian, same model as JavaScript Date.  Pure-loft; identical results on interp, --native, WASM.
tween 0.1.2 — Property tweens in exact integer time — eleven easing curves, chains and groups
web 0.5.0 — HTTP client + WebSocket client for loft — the natives are loft's `net` component, so the package builds no crate.
zttext 0.1.6 — A text engine for loft: piece-table content core, transactional undo, and portable layout with measurement injected
